    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"This report is provided as a reference guide to define the basic graphical user interface (GUI) responses needed to perform forward or inverse modeling of plane-wave electromagnetic (EM) data using an IBM compatible personal computer (PC). The underlying model used is a one-dimensional (1-D) horizontal layered earth with parameters being the layer resistivities and thicknesses below the earth's surface. Details of the geophysical and mathematical modeling are given by many authors (e.g., see Ward and Hohmann, 1988, and Wait, 1962, for a theoretical treatment of the 1-D plane-wave problem), and therefore will not be repeated here. The program in this report is named INVPW (for INVersion of Plane-Wave data).\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
